<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title> CSS Position Links & Lists</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #f5f5f5;
        }
        h1 {
            text-align: center;
        }
        h2 {
            margin-top: 40px;
        }
        .static-box {
            position: static;
            width: 200px;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: lightblue;
            border: 2px solid blue;
        }
        .relative-box {
            position: relative;
            left: 50px;
            top: 20px;

            width: 200px;
            padding: 20px;

            background-color: lightgreen;
            border: 2px solid green;
        }
        .parent {
            position: relative;

            width: 500px;
            height: 200px;

            background-color: lightgray;
            border: 2px solid black;
        }

        .absolute-box {
            position: absolute;

            right: 20px;
            bottom: 20px;

            padding: 20px;

            background-color: orange;
            border: 2px solid red;
        }
        .fixed-box {
            position: fixed;

            bottom: 20px;
            right: 20px;

            padding: 15px 25px;

            background-color: purple;
            color: white;

            border-radius: 8px;
        }
        .sticky-menu {
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;

            padding: 15px;

            background-color: black;
            color: white;

            text-align: center;
        }
        .links a {
            display: inline-block;

            padding: 10px 20px;
            margin: 5px;

            background-color: blue;
            color: white;

            text-decoration: none;

            border-radius: 5px;
        }
        .links a:hover {
            background-color: green;
        }
        .links a:visited {
            color: white;
        }
        .links a:active {
            background-color: red;
        }
        .unordered {
            list-style-type: square;
        }
        .ordered {
            list-style-type: upper-roman;
        }
        .custom-list {
            list-style-type: none;
            padding: 0;
        }

        .custom-list li {
            padding: 10px;
            margin: 5px;

            background-color: lightyellow;
            border: 1px solid orange;
        }
        .menu {
            list-style-type: none;

            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;

            text-align: center;
        }

        .menu li {
            display: inline-block;
        }

        .menu li a {
            display: block;

            padding: 15px 25px;

            background-color: #333;
            color: white;

            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .menu li a:hover {
            background-color: blue;
        }
        .content {
            height: 700px;
            padding: 20px;
        }

    </style>
</head>

<body>


    <h1>CSS Position Links and Lists</h1>
    <h2>1. Static Position</h2>

    <div class="static-box">
        This is Static Position
    </div>
    <h2>2. Relative Position</h2>

    <div class="relative-box">
        This box uses Relative Position
    </div>
    <h2>3. Absolute Position</h2>

    <div class="parent">

        <p>Parent Container</p>

        <div class="absolute-box">
            Absolute Box
        </div>

    </div>
    <h2>4. Sticky Position</h2>

    <div class="sticky-menu">
        Sticky Navigation Menu
    </div>
    <h2>5. CSS Links</h2>

    <div class="links">

        <a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">
            Google
        </a>

        <a href="https://www.youtube.com" target="_blank">
            YouTube
        </a>

        <a href="https://www.github.com" target="_blank">
            GitHub
        </a>

    </div>
    <h2>6. Unordered List</h2>

    <ul class="unordered">

        <li>HTML</li>
        <li>CSS</li>
        <li>JavaScript</li>
        <li>Python</li>

    </ul>

    <h2>7. Ordered List</h2>

    <ol class="ordered">

        <li>Learn HTML</li>
        <li>Learn CSS</li>
        <li>Learn JavaScript</li>
        <li>Learn Python</li>

    </ol>
    <h2>8. Custom List</h2>

    <ul class="custom-list">

        <li>Frontend Development</li>
        <li>Backend Development</li>
        <li>Database</li>
        <li>Full Stack Development</li>

    </ul>
    <h2>9. Horizontal Navigation Menu</h2>

    <ul class="menu">

        <li>
            <a href="#">Home</a>
        </li>

        <li>
            <a href="#">About</a>
        </li>

        <li>
            <a href="#">Services</a>
        </li>

        <li>
            <a href="#">Contact</a>
        </li>

    </ul>

    <div class="content">

        <h2>Scroll Down</h2>

        <p>
            This extra content is added to demonstrate
            sticky and fixed positioning.
        </p>

        <p>
            Scroll the page and observe the navigation</p>
    <div class="fixed-box">Notification</div>


</body>
</html>
